          "date": "2026-11-19 11:20:53.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-19674 tests: unload LNet on remote nodes after sanity-lnet",
        "message": "LU-19674 tests: unload LNet on remote nodes after sanity-lnet\n\nA sanity-lnet router test that fails skips cleanup_router_test. Its\nrouters and remote peer then keep the extra net, the routes and\nlnet_selftest. cleanup_testsuite cleans only the local node, so the\nnext suite mounts Lustre on nodes with that configuration. In\nfull-part-1 sessions where test_257 failed, the second client then\nnever sent an RPC to the servers, and ost-pools test_25 hung in\nclients_up.\n\nUnload the modules on all remote nodes in cleanup_testsuite, as a\nrouter test that passes does for the nodes it used.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet,ost-pools\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Iaf1d2bf35e7aa7fd5ce1b1f7d4cf934fcb4677aa\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
